  "summary": "RPO N14 side mounted exhaust (side pipes): the muffler and tail pipe assembly runs along the rocker below the doors, covered by a ribbed shield (side pipe cover). The muffler hangs from the frame on rubber insulators with a bolt, retainer, washers and nut, plus a rear bracket screwed to the frame outer member; the cover is screwed to the body sill along its top edge and held by a nut at the front and a clamp-type bracket at the rear. Note: N14 was cancelled for 1970 (see N14 A1).",
